/**
 * Historical snapshot of a product's state at a specific point in time. This
 * schema captures immutable versioned data of product attributes, pricing,
 * inventory status, and metadata as they existed when the snapshot was created.
 * Snapshots are automatically generated whenever product information is
 * modified via the IShoppingMallProduct.IUpdate request, providing a complete
 * audit trail for compliance, dispute resolution, and historical analysis.
 *
 * Each snapshot record contains a snapshot of the product's entire state at
 * creation, including base product properties, variant configurations, pricing
 * levels, inventory counts, and category assignments. The snapshot is a frozen
 * representation that never changes after creation and is linked to the
 * product's unique ID and the exact timestamp of the change.
 *
 * This schema is used in two operations: GET
 * /products/{productId}/snapshots/{snapshotId} to retrieve individual
 * historical records, and as the items in the paginated response from GET
 * /admin/products/{productId}/snapshots to list all historical versions for a
 * product. The data is sourced exclusively from the
 * shopping_mall_product_snapshots table and reflects the exact state of the
 * product at the moment of change, independent of any subsequent
 * modifications.
 *
 * Important: Snapshot data must be treated as read-only and immutable. No
 * operations modify or delete existing snapshots.
 *
 * Note: While product_variants, product_attributes, and inventory tracking are
 * referenced, the snapshot contains only the actual values that were present at
 * the time of creation, not references to live entities. These values are
 * stored as serialized, fixed property values within the snapshot
 *
 * @autobe Generated by AutoBE - https://github.com/wrtnlabs/autobe
 */
